-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----
Hash: SHA512

annotations:
  artifacthub.io/changes: |
    - kind: fixed
      description: "Lowered the edge's EDGE_WIDTH_CACHE_SIZE default from 10,000,000 to 2,500,000 entries. A full natural-width store costs about 180 bytes per entry on top of a ~400 MiB baseline, so 10M entries needed about 2.1 GiB and could never fit the 1 GiB edge memory limit: an edge that ran long enough to fill its store was OOMKilled and started again with an empty one. 2.5M fits the 1 GiB limit with headroom. If you set a larger size, raise edge.resources.limits.memory with it."
    - kind: added
      description: "SIZING.md: \"Edge memory and the natural-width store\" gives the memory formula, a table of store sizes and matching memory limits, and the imageengine_edge_kvcache_* metrics that show whether the store is big enough. CUSTOMIZATIONS.md and TROUBLESHOOTING.md (edge OOMKilled after running for days) point to it."
  artifacthub.io/signKey: |
    fingerprint: C3A55111ED91FEDE4A82A4B4463266060957C4B3
